folien (Folien) — Debian package notes
=====================================

Layout
  /opt/folien/app            application (replaced on every upgrade)
  /opt/folien/bin/scm        Scheme runtime launcher (bundled scm.jar)
  /etc/folien/config.scm     configuration (created on first install, kept)
  /etc/default/folien        optional: JAVA_OPTS="-Xmx2g"
  /var/lib/folien/           data-dir: assets/ (images, videos), backups/,
                             bundles/ (cache), tmp/
  folien.service + health/restart/maintenance/backup timers; logs in journald

First install
  1. Database (local or remote PostgreSQL):
       sudo -u postgres createuser -P folien
       sudo -u postgres createdb -O folien folien
  2. Edit /etc/folien/config.scm: db-* credentials, url-prefix if the app
     is not at the host root. The service starts only once db-password is
     no longer "change-me".
  3. The first admin (applies the migrations):
       sudo -u folien folien-admin seed-admin <name>
  4. systemctl start folien.service folien-health.timer folien-restart.timer \
       folien-maintenance.timer folien-backup.timer
  5. Reverse proxy with TLS in front: /usr/share/doc/folien/nginx.conf.example
     (client_max_body_size for uploads; buffering stays off for the event
     streams of presenting).

Upgrades
  apt install ./folien_<version>_all.deb — migrations run when the service
  starts.

Backups
  folien-backup.timer writes database dumps to /var/lib/folien/backups
  nightly (backup-keep of them). Back up /var/lib/folien (dumps and
  assets) with your file backup. Restore: gunzip -c <dump> | psql folien,
  then put /var/lib/folien back.

Tools
  folien-admin <script>: seed-admin, gen-secret, maintenance, backup, server.
